OL,3,A'Ghost particles' from space telescope
OL,4,Awins physics Nobel
OL,5,
OL,6,FBelgian physicist Prof Francis Halzen
OL,7,Fhas won the Nobel Prize in Physics for
OL,8,Fhis pioneering work on an observatory
OL,9,Fthat detects particles from space,
OL,10,Fshedding light on the distant universe.
OL,12,FHalzen led the development of IceCube
OL,13,Fat the South Pole, which uses a cubic
OL,14,Fkilometre of Antarctic ice fitted with
OL,15,Flight sensors to detect particles
OL,16,Fcalled neutrinos. These carry
OL,17,Finformation about violent, high-energy
OL,18,Fprocesses in the cosmos.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
